  "note": "All windows are TRAILING and INCLUDE the current day: window(t, w) = days t-w+1 .. t. At the start of the series the window is truncated to the days that exist (means divide by the number of days present, max / min / sum over the days present) - there is no NaN. They are computed per coarse point on the unshifted Open-Meteo series (the lapse shift is applied later, per pixel).",
